---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';


const path = '/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-attentive';
const title = 'Yotpo Email & SMS to Attentive for Shopify: Migration Assessment';
const desc = 'One-time subscriber transfer and a separate loyalty integration handoff after Yotpo messaging retirement.';
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I keep using Yotpo Email & SMS?",
    "answer": "No. The messaging product is retired; assess a replacement sender and keep Reviews and Loyalty as separate decisions."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should decide whether Attentive fits?",
    "answer": "One-time subscriber transfer and a separate loyalty integration handoff. Use the proposed acceptance cases in this guide before approving production enrollment."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does importing contacts restore every journey?",
    "answer": "No. Permissions, message history, dynamic segments and waiting automation contacts need separate reconciliation. Import success is not a sending approval."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I also consider Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "Include Sequenzy if it is on your shortlist, using the same consent, Shopify event and operating-cost requirements. This page has not verified its current plan terms or migration tooling; it does not establish a price or feature advantage."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a> / Yotpo to Attentive</nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="catalog-kicker">Migration assessment</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS to Attentive for Shopify</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">One-time subscriber transfer and a separate loyalty integration handoff. This guide proposes checks for a replacement program; it does not report merchant tests or measured outcomes.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>A retired sender changes the decision</h2>
      <p>Yotpo announced messaging retirement for the end of 2025. Its application now displays a decommission notice. Compare destinations and recovery options, rather than choosing to remain on that sender. <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo lifecycle notice</a>.</p>
      <h2>Understand the partner route</h2>
      <p>Attentive documents a Shopify-mediated, one-time Yotpo subscriber migration, with static lists imported as static segments and dynamic segments rebuilt. Its guide requires SMS setup and subscriber-list certification. Because Yotpo messaging is now decommissioned, ask Attentive which recovery path remains available for your account before relying on that older procedure. A partnership announcement does not establish present access.</p>
      <h2>Rebuild membership, not just names</h2>
      <p>Use a proposed retail signup exercise: compare a store QR subscriber, an ecommerce subscriber and a person who opted out after the original export. Record channel permission and source for each. Recreate a dynamic recent-purchaser segment from destination order data; do not treat an imported static snapshot as a rule that will keep updating. A matching audience total cannot demonstrate permission accuracy.</p>
      <h2>Separate Reviews from Loyalty</h2>
      <p>Keep review collection and on-site display under an explicit owner. For Loyalty, list tier changes, points reminders and signup rewards separately from Reviews events. Request the actual integration version and event payloads before rebuilding journeys. If replacing an older loyalty connector, inventory its journeys and segments; disabling a connector alone is not evidence that old message paths were removed.</p>
      <h2>Proposed cutover acceptance</h2>
      <p>Prepare new capture links and inspect old QR codes, social links and embedded forms. Confirm where new opt-outs go after the one-time transfer. In a controlled test, an existing subscriber must not receive a new-subscriber incentive merely because of import; a genuine new signup should enter the intended welcome journey. Review number changes with Attentive and the responsible compliance owner. Do not infer that migrating subscriber records also ports a sending number.</p>
      <h2>Decide on operating ownership</h2>
      <p>Attentive merits assessment when you want a documented Yotpo migration route and coordinated email/SMS operation. Ask for a named owner for audience reconciliation, message approval and incident suspension. Compare a written scope of migration support with the work your team must do. Keep outbound campaigns paused when unresolved permission differences remain; restarting the retired Yotpo sender is not a recovery plan.</p>
      <h2>History and active queues need different treatment</h2>
      <p>Keep Shopify order history, Yotpo message history and consent evidence as distinct records. For every still-active destination queue, record its sender, next action and stop condition. Waiting contacts are operational state, not simply an audience export. Reconstruct only the messages still justified by current purchase and permission data. If an import or event mapping fails, pause the replacement journey and reconcile it; the decommissioned service is not a rollback destination.</p>
      <h2>Price the work you will retain</h2>
      <p>Request current plan terms for the eligible audience, expected sends, channel usage and required integrations. Add retained Reviews/Loyalty charges and one-time reconstruction labor separately. Compare a normal month with your own peak calendar. No supplier price, revenue uplift or payback period is assumed here. A lower messaging quote can still leave more manual work if historical data or queue state cannot be recovered.</p>
      <h2>Evidence and remaining limits</h2>
      <p>Checked November 24, 2026: <a class="link" href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/41028229226900-Migrate-your-email-and-SMS-program-from-Yotpo-to-Attentive">Attentive implementation documentation</a>. The acceptance designs above are editorial proposals. Account access, recovery availability, actual event payloads, legal sufficiency of permission records and live delivery remain untested. Obtain the missing evidence before enabling the affected journeys.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="/guides/migration">Migration guide</a> · <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing-models">Pricing models</a></p>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-attentive">Postscript vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-postscript">Yotpo vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-attentive">Omnisend vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Yotpo to Attentive FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
